{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "The harsh fluorescent light of his bedroom felt…wrong. Not physically uncomfortable, just *wrong*. Mark blinked, trying to focus on the posters of video game characters plastered on his walls. He’d always loved those games, losing himself in their worlds. But something felt different. The way the light glinted off his desk, the subtle hum of the refrigerator – it was all too perfect, too pristine. He reached out to touch a poster of a hulking warrior, and his fingers passed right through it. A jolt, like static electricity, ran up his arm. He looked down at his hands – they were strangely smooth, almost…digital. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Player Mark initiating level 1.\" Panic clawed at his throat. This wasn't his room. This wasn't his life.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling strangely solid beneath his feet. The room shimmered around him, the posters morphing into detailed, three-dimensional representations of the game world he’d been playing last night. A pixelated knight, clad in shining armor, materialized in the corner, its visor glowing. \"Welcome, Mark,\" the knight boomed, its voice synthesized and slightly tinny. \"You are now the hero of Aethelgard. Your quest begins now.\" Mark felt a wave of nausea wash over him. He was trapped, inside a video game. The implications were terrifying. He had to figure out how to survive, how to navigate this bizarre reality, and most importantly, how to find a way back to his own world, before he became just another NPC in someone else's digital adventure.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6729406118392944}, {"token": "▁harsh", "logprob": -1.6302294731140137}, {"token": "▁fluorescent", "logprob": -0.6193198561668396}, {"token": "▁light", "logprob": -1.2327239513397217}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.4009840190410614}, {"token": "▁his", "logprob": -0.462116062